    </format>
    <page-count>45</page-count>
    <keywords>
      <kw>DHCP</kw>
      <kw>DHCPv4</kw>
    </keywords>
    <abstract>
      <p>The Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP) provides a framework for passing configuration information to hosts on a TCPIP network.  DHCP is based on the Bootstrap Protocol (BOOTP), adding the capability of automatic allocation of reusable network addresses and additional configuration options. [STANDARDS-TRACK]</p>
